      "body": "## Purpose\n\n`kv_postprocess_layout_on_receive` rewrites the blocks that were just copied\ninto the local cache so that their layout matches what the local attention\nbackend expects. It gathers them, permutes the two inner dimensions and writes\nthem back:\n\n```python\nblocks_to_update = cache.index_select(0, indices)      # line 283\ntarget_shape = list(blocks_to_update.shape)\ntarget_shape[0] = -1\ninv_order = [0, 1, 3, 2, 4] if blocks_to_update.ndim == 5 else [0, 2, 1, 3]\nsrc_shape = tuple(target_shape[i] for i in inv_order)\nblocks_to_update = cache.index_select(0, indices)      # line 288 - identical\npermuted_blocks = blocks_to_update.reshape(src_shape).permute(*inv_order)\ncache.index_copy_(0, indices, permuted_blocks)\n```\n\nLine 288 repeats line 283 verbatim and immediately overwrites its result with\nan identical tensor, so the reshape/permute/copy are unaffected by it. The\nfirst call is needed (`target_shape`/`inv_order` are derived from its shape and\nndim); the second is not.\n\n`index_select` is a full gather of every received block, and this runs on the\ndecode side for each received block set, so the duplicate doubles a temporary\nallocation proportional to the transferred KV. Deleting the statement is\nbehaviour-preserving; the only observable difference is one fewer gather.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n`tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_kv_postprocess_layout_on_receive.py` wraps a\nreal `torch` cache tensor so the gathers and the write-back are counted, and\nruns the helper for both the 4D and the 5D cache layout:\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_kv_postprocess_layout_on_receive.py -q\n```\n\nBesides the call counts it also pins the operation's contract - a layout fix-up\nis a permutation, so the received blocks must keep their multiset of values and\nuntouched blocks must be left alone - which guards against a future change that\n\"optimises\" the remaining gather away or reorders the permutation.\n\n## Test Result\n\n```\ntests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_kv_postprocess_layout_on_receive.py ..   [100%]\n2 passed\n```\n\nOn the unpatched tree the same test reports two gathers and fails:\n\n```\nFAILED .../test_kv_postprocess_layout_on_receive.py::test_the_received_blocks_are_gathered_once[4d_cache]\nFAILED .../test_kv_postprocess_layout_on_receive.py::test_the_received_blocks_are_gathered_once[5d_cache]\n2 failed\n```\n\nTested on main (`105a4e09`), Linux x86_64 / Python 3.12, CPU-only `torch`.\n",
